  honeycomb_run_query: Tool {
    id: 'honeycomb_run_query',
    description: "Time-series data query and aggregation API. Supports compound queries (query math): name calculations, add per-calculation filters, and combine them with formulas (e.g., $errors / $total * 100). IMPORTANT: For time parameters, prefer human-readable formats like '-24h', 'last 7 days', or '2023-11-15' over Unix epoch integers. When data is sampled, results include sampling metadata. COUNT, SUM, AVG, percentiles, HEATMAP, CONCURRENCY, RATE_SUM, RATE_AVG are weighted by sample rate by default. COUNT_DISTINCT, MIN, MAX, RATE_MAX are not. Use usage_mode=true to disable all sample rate correction and see raw event counts. METRICS DATASETS: Temporal aggregation (LAST, SUMMARIZE, INCREASE) is applied automatically based on metric type — do not attempt to use these as calculated_field expressions. RATE_SUM, RATE_AVG, RATE_MAX, CONCURRENCY, and bare COUNT (without column) are NOT allowed on metrics datasets. Use SUM, AVG, MAX, or percentiles on metric fields instead of COUNT. COUNT_DATAPOINTS and HISTOGRAM_COUNT are only allowed in metrics datasets. HISTOGRAM_COUNT extracts the count from histogram metric columns. For histogram metrics, use AVG/P50/P99/MAX/HEATMAP directly on the histogram column name (e.g., P99(http.server.duration)).",
    inputSchema: JsonSchemaWrapper { '~standard': [Object] },
    outputSchema: undefined,
    suspendSchema: undefined,
    resumeSchema: undefined,
    requestContextSchema: undefined,
    execute: [AsyncFunction (anonymous)],
    mastra: undefined,
    requireApproval: false,
    strict: undefined,
    providerOptions: undefined,
    toModelOutput: undefined,
    transform: undefined,
    mcp: undefined,
